            {
              "text": "In Perth’s prestige real estate market—concentrated across the **Western Suburbs** (*Peppermint Grove, Dalkeith, Cottesloe, Swanbourne, Nedlands, Mosman Park, City Beach*) and premier riverfront enclaves (*Applecross, Attadale, South Perth*)—a large percentage of luxury homes trade **off-market or via discreet private placement**. \n\nBecause traditional selling agents are legally bound to achieve the highest price for the vendor, high-net-worth individuals, expats, and family offices increasingly engage **independent buyer’s advocates and acquisition advisors** to secure off-market access, maintain privacy, and conduct uncompromised valuation and due diligence.\n\nThe leading buyer’s advocacy firms and advisors specializing in Perth’s luxury and prestige residential sector include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. CPA Private (Capital Property Advisory)\n* **Prestige Focus:** Cottesloe, Dalkeith, Swanbourne, Peppermint Grove, and City Beach.\n* **Overview:** Capital Property Advisory operates a dedicated, high-end division called **CPA Private**, specifically designed as a discreet, white-glove acquisition service for luxury home buyers, high-net-worth individuals, and family offices.\n* **Strengths:** \n  * Proprietary data and research framework (*CPAnalytics*™) combined with advisory-led structuring.\n  * Highly focused on strict confidentiality, eliminating open-home viewings and public listings.\n  * Managing Director Matthew Hughes is heavily decorated in the property advisory space (PIPA National Property Investment Adviser of the Year recipient).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Cohen Handler Perth\n* **Prestige Focus:** Perth’s “Golden Triangle” (Western Suburbs) and coastal luxury.\n* **Overview:** Founded nationally by Simon Cohen (featured on *Luxe Listings Australia*) and spearheaded locally in WA by lead buyers agents like Justin Dixon (a REIWA Buyer’s Agent of the Year finalist), Cohen Handler is one of Australia’s most prominent luxury buyer’s agencies.\n* **Strengths:**\n  * Exceptional national brand cachet and aggressive off-market acquisition reach.\n  * Extensive relationships with Perth’s top listing agents, ensuring private access before homes hit public portals.\n  * Specializes in multi-million-dollar transactions, interstate executive relocations, and private negotiations.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Resolve Property Solutions\n* **Prestige Focus:** Established Western Suburbs, Swan River foreshore, and premium coastal pockets.\n* **Overview:** Led by Peter Gavalas, Resolve Property Solutions is a boutique, Perth-headquartered buyer’s agency with a strong market presence and top-tier client ratings.\n* **Strengths:**\n  * Hands-on, principal-led service where clients work directly with senior advisors rather than being handed off to junior associates.\n  * Strong local market commentary and deep familiarity with zoning, street-by-street micro-pricing, and heritage overlays in older, established suburbs.\n  * Excellent reputation for due diligence and private off-market sourcing.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Claudette Swift Buyer’s Agents\n* **Prestige Focus:** Luxury estates, architectural builds, and lifestyle acreage across Greater Perth and WA.\n* **Overview:** With over 30 years in the Western Australian property sector, Claudette Swift runs a dedicated consultancy tailored to discerning buyers seeking primary luxury residences and lifestyle properties.\n* **Strengths:**\n  * Caters specifically to buyers who require strict privacy and concierge-style service.\n  * Extensive tenure in the WA market translates into decades-long connections with high-end developers, architects, and private owners.\n  * Highly experienced in handling complex contractual terms and off-market viewings.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Verve Buyers Agency\n* **Prestige Focus:** Western Suburbs enclaves (Subiaco, Nedlands, Claremont, Cottesloe, Dalkeith).\n* **Overview:** Verve deploys hyper-local neighborhood specialists (such as Western Suburbs specialist Luca Albano) to represent buyers looking for high-end character homes, riverfront residences, and luxury downsizer apartments.\n* **Strengths:**\n  * Direct street-level approaches (canvassing non-listed homeowners directly in specific target streets if no suitable stock is available).\n  * In-depth understanding of strata rules and construction quality for premium apartments versus heritage restrictions for older riverside character homes.\n\n---\n\n### Important Distinction: Dedicated Buyer's Advocates vs. Prestige Sales Agencies\nIf you are buying prestige property in Perth, ensure you differentiate between:\n1. **Independent Buyer’s Advocates** (e.g., *CPA Private, Cohen Handler, Resolve*): They are paid **solely by you** and legally obligated to act in your best financial interest.\n2. **Prestige Selling Agencies** (e.g., *William Porteous Properties International, Ray White Dalkeith | Claremont led by Vivien Yap, Shellabears, Mack Hall Real Estate*): These agencies control a large portion of Perth’s luxury listings. While keeping in contact with their lead agents can grant you early looks at upcoming pocket listings, **their legal and fiduciary duty is to the seller**, not the buyer.\n\n---\n\n### What to Look for When Choosing an Advisor in Perth\n* **REBAA / REIWA Membership:** Check whether they are an accredited member of the **Real Estate Buyers Agent Association of Australia (REBAA)** or licensed with **REIWA** (Real Estate Institute of Western Australia).\n* **Off-Market Transaction Rate:** Ask what percentage of their prestige transactions in the last 12–24 months were genuinely unlisted or pre-market. In Perth's top-tier market, this figure should ideally exceed 40–50%.\n* **Exclusivity & Capacity Limits:** A reputable luxury advocate should only take on 1–2 active briefs at a time in the same price/suburb bracket to prevent bidding against their own clients.",
